1
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:12,000
She's more than a toy. She's family.

2
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:18,000
M3GAN is a science fiction, horror film directed by Gerard Johnstone.

3
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:24,000
A brilliant toy company roboticist uses artificial intelligence to develop M3GAN, a
life-like doll programmed to emotionally bond with her newly orphaned niece.

4
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:30,000
But when the doll's programming works too well, she becomes
overprotective of her new friend with terrifying results.

5
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:36,000
Gemma, played by Allison Williams.

6
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:42,000
Cady, played by Violet McGraw.

7
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:48,000
M3gan, played by Amie Donald.

8
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:54,000
M3gan (voice), played by Jenna Davis.

9
00:45:54,000 --> 00:46:00,000
David, played by Ronny Chieng.

10
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
Cole, played by Brian Jordan Alvarez.

11
00:56:06,000 --> 00:56:12,000
M3GAN (pronounced "Megan") is a 2022 American science fiction horror film with black comedy elements about an artificially
intelligent doll who develops self-awareness and becomes hostile toward anyone who comes between her and her human companion.

12
01:01:12,000 --> 01:01:18,000
It was directed by Gerard Johnstone from a screenplay by Akela
Cooper, based on a story by Cooper and James Wan.

13
01:06:18,000 --> 01:06:24,000
Allison Williams and Violet McGraw star, Amie Donald physically
portrays M3GAN, and Jenna Davis voices the character.

14
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:30,000
It is the first installment in the M3GAN franchise.

15
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
M3GAN premiered in Los Angeles on December 7, 2022, and Universal Pictures
theatrically released it in the United States on January 6, 2023.

16
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:42,000
The film grossed over $181 million worldwide against a budget of $12 million and received
generally positive reviews from critics, who praised its campy blend of horror and humor.

17
01:26:42,000 --> 01:26:48,000
A sequel, M3GAN 2.0, was theatrically released in June 2025,
and a spin-off, SOULM8TE, is set to follow.

18
01:31:48,000 --> 01:31:54,000
The film explores themes of android, artificial intelligence (a.i.),
killer robot, aunt niece relationship, evil doll.

19
01:36:54,000 --> 01:37:00,000
The tone is dark and emotional and thought_provoking.
